  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A nanoscale, functionally graded amorphous Ti/Zr-containing coating on CoCrFeNi will provide adaptive low-friction and low-wear behavior from room temperature to 800 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At room temperature, the amorphous coating will possess intrinsic lubricity.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The disordered structure and smooth surface of the amorphous coating will reduce low-temperature friction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperatures up to 800 °C, the coating will transform in situ into a dense oxide glaze.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC10241162::web::033::adaptive_friction_interface_protection"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The high-temperature glaze will be enriched in oxides of the Ti and Zr additives, including TiO2 and ZrO2.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::033::adaptive_friction_interface_protection"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A dense oxide glaze can reduce adhesion and minimize adhesive and oxidative wear at high temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC10241162::web::033::adaptive_friction_interface_protection"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Glaze layers rich in selected oxidizable elements can provide anti-wear and oxidation resistance during high-temperature sliding.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::033::adaptive_friction_interface_protection"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing the concentration of suitable oxidizable additives can accelerate formation and densification of a protective glaze.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::033::adaptive_friction_interface_protection"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi alloy has good room-temperature friction performance.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bare CoCrFeNi develops increased friction and wear as temperature approaches 800 °C.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The high-temperature deterioration of bare CoCrFeNi is caused by oxidation, phase instability, and surface degradation.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to bare CoCrFeNi, the coated alloy will have a lower coefficient of friction throughout the complete room-temperature-to-800 °C range.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to bare CoCrFeNi, the coated alloy will have a lower wear rate throughout the complete room-temperature-to-800 °C range.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The greatest improvement over bare CoCrFeNi will occur between 600 and 800 °C because a protective glaze forms.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC10241162::web::033::adaptive_friction_interface_protection"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adaptive interface protection can sustain low wear over a room-temperature-to-800 °C sliding regime.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed behavior is applicable at a normal load around 30 N.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed behavior is applicable at sliding speeds around 1–5 mm/s.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
